          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>EXECUTIVE DECISION SUMMARY</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Demand Surge:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> Adding 276 units in Week 4 restores 100% modeled fulfillment, eliminates 276 shortage units, and reduces illustrative economic exposure by $16,888.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Supplier Delay:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> Expediting the original shipment restores 100% modeled fulfillment with $2,500 in illustrative exposure, compared with $8,420 for the Week 3 bridge alternative.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Recommendation:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> Prioritize interventions satisfying the 98% fill-rate and zero-shortage-week requirements while evaluating economic exposure and execution feasibility.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12' italic='true'>Results reflect hypothetical planning scenarios, not realized financial savings.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
